<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/10/M5-MacBook-Pro.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="brief" align="left" style="float:left;margin:0 20px 20px 0;width:160px;height:auto;" /><em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman has walked back somewhat on his previous reporting that Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/23/macbook-ultra-coming-soon-touchscreen-5-changes/">upcoming touchscreen OLED MacBook Pro</a> will be thinner than current models. "I don't think it'll be significantly thinner in the end," he <a href="https://x.com/markgurman/status/2107961914404061318?s=20">posted on X</a> late Wednesday in reply to a question about the machine, which is expected to launch on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/08/apple-october-27-macbook-pro/">October 27</a>.<br/>
<br/>
In October 2025, Gurman <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-10-16/apple-readies-high-end-macbook-pro-with-touch-hole-punch-screen">reported</a> that the OLED MacBook Pro models would have "thinner and lighter" frames. Then again in <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2025-11-09/apple-iphone-satellite-plans-image-texting-third-party-apps-low-cost-macbook-mhrq10p2">November 2025</a>, he said the touchscreen models would have "a thinner chassis." Now it seems that they will only be "significantly lighter," per Gurman's <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2026-10-04/apple-s-john-ternus-leads-design-touch-screen-oled-macbook-pro-gets-lighter">October 2026 newsletter</a>. It seems thinner and lighter do not necessarily go hand in hand.<div class="linkback">Related Roundup: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a></div><div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/oled/">OLED</a></div><div class="linkback">Buyer's Guide: <a href="https://buyersguide.macrumors.com/#MacBook_Pro_16">MacBook Pro (Caution)</a></div><div class="linkback">Related Forum: <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/forums/macbook-pro.90">MacBook Pro</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/08/oled-macbook-pro-wont-be-thinner/">Gurman: OLED MacBook Pro Won&#039;t Be &#039;Significantly Thinner&#039;</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/gurman-oled-macbook-pro-wont-be-significantly-thinner.2491307/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>